WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.770
Noa, why did you bring us to this virtual world?

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:27.570
Why are you so hostile towards me?

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:33.740
The answer is that you're Gozaburo's son.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.970
But that only raises more questions about you.

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:42.740
I will uncover the truth and rescue Mokuba!

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:49.020
The Big Five's Counterattack

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.180
After losing your duels, you tried to take their bodies by force.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.870
Such pathetic adults.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.480
I'm done with you.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.880
Never show your faces again.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.400
P-Please wait, Noa.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.780
We desperately want bodies.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.120
Fresh young bodies.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.240
Bodies?  I thought you got one.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.080
That's Ota's.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.230
We still need four more.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:30.930
Wait a sec.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.500
Noa is right.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.150
You shouldn't have lost your duels.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.240
What?

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.000
I acquired Honda's body.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.620
I got it by winning my duel.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.850
So this body belongs to me!

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.710
You won your duel?

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.480
Nonsense.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.720
You lost!

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.720
That's right!  You lost your duel!

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:58.660
We all have a right to claim that body!

00:02:58.660 --> 00:02:59.660
What?

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:04.330
Please!  Stop arguing in front of me!

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.330
But Noa!

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.840
Fine.  I'll give you one last chance.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:18.910
Your opponent will be Yugi Muto.  Seto Kaiba thinks he's his only rival.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:24.350
If you win the duel, I'll give you five bodies.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.950
So no complaints.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.570
Thank you very much, Noa.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:32.560
I won't let your good judgment go to waste.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.570
I promise to succeed this time!

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:46.640
What?  Noa is the son of Kaiba Corporation's former president?

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.290
Yeah.  That's what he said.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.450
But why did he only kidnap Mokuba?

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:58.450
Yeah.  Noa is very hostile towards Kaiba.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:02.550
So he took Mokuba to torment Kaiba-

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:04.920
Wait!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.790
What are you doing?

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.860
Where are you going?

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:12.030
If you're going to save Mokuba, we'll go with you!

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.030
I thought I told you.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:14.970
What?

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.610
This is me and my brother's problem.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.540
It doesn't concern you.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:20.940
Move!

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.880
It does concern us!

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:32.050
They brought us to this weird place too!

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.970
Besides...  Mokuba is our friend!

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.790
It's normal to worry about a friend!

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.350
Then you should worry about him.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:50.770
Honda!

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.700
No.  That's not Honda!

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.710
That's my body!  Give it back!

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:08.450
Ota, Kaiba Corporation's factory manager, possesses Honda's body.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.110
I'm not the only one.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.770
This is Honda's body...

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.770
But we're all inside!

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:18.960
The Big Five!

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.070
The Big Five?

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:29.680
Yugi Muto!  Duel us again!

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:34.310
I'll get your fresh young body this time!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.310
It's that penguin's voice!

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:41.180
Fine!  But if I win, give back Honda's body!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.190
Okay.  I promise.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.760
Wait a second!

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.900
Don't make promises on your own!

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:54.520
And why do you get to use the body that I acquired?

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.430
Stop complaining.  You can have it back when we get our own bodies.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:05.320
Since I'm the lawyer, leave the negotiations to me.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:11.120
Let's duel, Yugi!

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.420
Yeah!  Let's do it!

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.170
I'll duel you!

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.660
Wait!

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:26.240
Since you share that body, this duel is 5-on-1!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.080
That's too unfair!

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.200
Let me duel too!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.170
Jonouchi...

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:36.910
I can't just sit and watch if Honda's body is at stake.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.910
Yeah.  Help me, Jonouchi.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:44.280
Jonouchi, you care so much about me!

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:45.920
I'm touched!

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.520
Understood.  Fine.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.520
Wait!  Then we're at a disadvantage!

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.120
Disadvantage?

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:59.620
Jonouchi will hinder Yugi, so it's favorable for us.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:02.030
He's a mediocre duelist.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:06.640
Since Jonouchi defeated you, you're not convincing me.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:10.550
Anyway, let me handle the negotiations.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.750
I have an idea.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:16.010
So this'll be a tag duel.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:21.740
But we'll be a disadvantage because you'll have more life points.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:29.860
So we'll have 8000 life points, which equals your combined life points.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:31.030
Okay?

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.800
No wonder you're a corrupt lawyer.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.760
But we have no choice.  Fine.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.770
Build your decks.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.150
Mai...

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.770
Hang in there, Mai.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:56.640
I have to retrieve Honda's body first.

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:03.890
Then I'll get out of here, defeat Marik and return you to normal.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.930
My Deck Master is Dark Magician!

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.260
Mine is Flame Swordsman!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:26.100
We can choose one Deck Master every turn.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:32.190
I, Konosuke Oshita, will fight using Deepsea Warrior!

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:35.290
I'm counting on you, Yugi and Jonouchi!

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.300
Don't worry.  I know they'll win.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.300
Yeah.  You'll get your body back soon.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.900
Thanks, you guys!

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.640
You too, Shizuka.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:48.140
Do your best, brother.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.740
Here I go!

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.370
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:55.770 --> 00:09:01.000
I activate the Field Spell, A Legendary Ocean!

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:09.690
Run, Shizuka!

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.690
Whoa!  A Field Spell already?

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:16.200
I summon The Legendary Fisherman!

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.440
That's Ryota Kajiki's favorite monster!

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:28.570
Wait a sec.  That monster is Level 5.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:31.860
How can he summon it without tributing?

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:33.680
It's the Field Spell's effect.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:40.960
Yes.  A Legendary Ocean lowers a monster's Level by 1.

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:47.700
Level 5 monsters become Level 4, so I can summon them without tributing.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:53.700
His Deck Master, Deepsea Warrior, is good at using Water Attribute monsters.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:57.940
He's trying to get the advantage from the start.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.940
I end my turn.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.780
Be careful, Jonouchi.

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:05.860
Don't get caught up in his pace.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:10.560
I know.  After all, I didn't beat Ryota Kajiki by luck!

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.920
Yugi, let me go first.

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.160
My turn!

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:17.640
Here I go!  I summon Alligator's Sword!

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:23.530
In a tag duel, I can't attack on the first turn.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.850
I end my turn.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.700
Just wait, Honda.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:35.160
I promise to get your body back.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:36.930
My turn!

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:37.650
I draw!

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.600
I summon Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts in defense position!

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.200
I end my turn!

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.760
My turn.  I draw-

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.520
Listen, Oshita.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:55.180
Now that The Legendary Fisherman is out, it's my turn.

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.700
Wait a second!

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.700
I'm not done!

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.060
Silence!

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:06.460
Nightmare Penguin's Deck Master ability raises the attack points of Water Attribute monsters!

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.210
Leave this to me.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.620
I draw!

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:10.900
His voice changed!

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.550
A different one's in charge?

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:19.710
Yes.  55 year-old Shuzo Otaki's Nightmare Penguin will duel you.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:28.480
I'll defeat you and acquire that lovely girl's body.

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:33.300
Please, Yugi!  You must win!

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:47.150
A Legendary Ocean raises the attack and defense points of all Water Attribute monsters by 200.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:52.140
But in the ocean, The Legendary Fisherman isn't affected by spells.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.160
So his attack points don't change.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:59.520
The Legendary Fisherman attacks Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts!

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:09.140
A Deck Master's ability isn't a spell, so The Legendary Fisherman gains 200 attack points.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.020
Next, Catapult Turtle in defense position!

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:26.140
He summoned another Level 5 monster without tributing.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.160
I end my turn!

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:29.600
Damn.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:34.660
If we don't do something about A Legendary Ocean, we're in trouble!

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:35.960
Yeah.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:06.360
I'm Noa Kaiba.  Gozaburo Kaiba's only real son.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:13.900
Noa said that since I was similar to him, Gozaburo adopted me to be his fake rival.

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:19.560
But if that's true, Noa and I should be the same age.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:23.180
But he's a kid.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:39.570
There are two ways to explain this contradiction.

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:42.710
One: Everything is a lie.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:49.680
Two: Noa is dead, and he's a ghost.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:53.540
I'm talking about ghosts?

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:57.570
It seems Yugi's occult ideas are contagious.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.550
How dumb!

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:12.480
Damn!  I can't attack a monster that I can't see!

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.480
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.060
Kunai with Chain.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:25.310
Okay.  I can't use this on his Field Spell, but I can stop The Legendary Fisherman's attack.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.540
I set a card!

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.120
I'm counting on you, Mai.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:36.720
I summon Cyber Harpie!

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:41.990
And I switch Alligator's Sword to attack position!

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:43.720
I end my turn!

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:45.230
My turn!

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.240
I draw!

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:54.740
I don't have any cards in my hand that can destroy his Field Spell.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.770
Jonouchi's set card...

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:00.240
I'll let Jonouchi handle this.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.160
I summon Mystical Elf in defense position!

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.520
I end my turn!

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:12.420
It's my turn.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:15.800
No.  It's still my turn.

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:17.660
You're not up yet.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:21.170
I draw!

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.300
I'm the one who'll defeat Yugi!

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:30.170
With The Legendary Fisherman!

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:33.370
Attack Mystical Elf!

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:36.380
Stop right there!

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:38.750
I activate my trap card!

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.750
Kunai with Chain!

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.490
Well done, Jonouchi!

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:54.240
Too bad.  Kunai with Chain switches The Legendary Fisherman to defense position.

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:59.930
And my monster gains 500 attack points.

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:03.700
Sheesh!  All you do is talk about Yugi!

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:06.440
But he's not the only one dueling!

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.810
What are you doing?

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:12.740
Play better!

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:16.050
Silence!  It's no big deal!

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:19.650
I set a monster!

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:21.640
I end my turn!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.880
Nice, Jonouchi!

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.460
Brother, you're incredible!

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:32.450
But they still have their Field Spell-  Screech!

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:34.970
They can't let their guard down-  Screech!

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.970
By the way, I've been thinking...

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:43.550
You keep screeching.  You're talking more like a monkey.

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:44.340
Are you okay?

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:46.710
Really?  Screech!

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:51.370
I'm talking like a monkey!  Screech!

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:54.350
I'm turning into a real monkey!  Screech!

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.250
Please, Jonouchi!

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:58.360
Get my body back soon!

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:00.290
Here I go!  My turn!

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:01.590
I draw!

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:08.700
All right!  I can use this to destroy their Field Spell!

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:12.900
It was a good decision to include Mai's cards in my deck.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:16.400
I activate the spell card, Harpie's Feather Duster!

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:24.210
A Legendary Ocean's field effect is gone!

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:25.960
Here I go!

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:30.640
Cyber Harpie, attack The Legendary Fisherman!

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:34.570
I'm not done!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.930
Next, I attack with Alligator's Sword!

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:38.940
Wait.

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:42.280
Catapult Turtle has 2000 defense points.

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:47.340
That's the same as Alligator's Sword equipped with Kunai with Chain.

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:52.390
So I'll destroy that one first.

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:53.860
Wait, Jonouchi!

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:55.040
It's dangerous!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.440
Don't worry.  Just watch, Yugi.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:58.940
I can do anything!

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:02.660
Alligator's Sword, destroy the set monster!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.730
Magician of Faith's Flip Effect activates!

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:14.970
I add a spell card in my graveyard to my hand.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:15.700
What?

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:19.710
Naturally, I'm getting this spell card back!

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:25.450
Oh no!  Just when I got rid of A Legendary Ocean, he got it back!

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.660
You should be more careful.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.180
Damn!  I end my turn!

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:33.840
Sorry, Yugi.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.420
I got carried away.

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:37.480
Forget it, Jonouchi.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:39.280
It's no big deal.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.160
My turn!  I draw!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:51.020
When I activate A Legendary Ocean and use Monster Reborn to resurrect The Legendary Fisherman next turn...

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.970
...everything will be perfect!

00:18:53.250 --> 00:19:00.900
This proves that an adult is superior to a kid!

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.350
Are you sure?

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:07.190
I'll show that I'm superior to you!

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:08.290
What?

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.080
I summon Kuriboh in defense position.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:16.460
I activate the spell card, Card Destruction!

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:25.270
You got A Legendary Ocean back, but it returns to the graveyard again.

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:26.950
Well done, Yugi!

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.270
You're incredible!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:34.810
Draw cards from your deck equal to the number you discarded.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:38.920
I end my turn.

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:41.640
Damn!  My tur-

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:44.560
That's enough.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.520
Your time is up.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:50.530
It's my turn.

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:52.260
He changed again!

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.770
Stop playing with my body!

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:59.610
This is very intense.

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:02.350
Haven't you noticed?

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:09.010
They're having a fierce duel, but no one has lost a single life point.

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:12.660
But that'll come to an end.

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:17.750
I, Chikuzen Ooka, will use Judge Man against you.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:22.630
It's only a matter of time until you have 0 life points.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:42.080
Mokuba!

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:43.930
Where are you?

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:46.480
Answer me!

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:51.990
Do you want to go back to him?

00:20:56.240 --> 00:21:00.230
No.  You're my only brother, Noa.

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:28.930
That's...

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:30.820
Kaiba Land?

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:49.330
The Big Five keep switching and attacking.

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:53.320
They're focusing their attack on Jonouchi.

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:57.220
Yugi can't counterattack, so he tries using traps.

00:21:57.220 --> 00:22:00.680
But Jonouchi is flustered because his traps are too obvious.

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:05.800
But would Yugi really do something so obvious without having a plan?

00:22:06.060 --> 00:22:09.880
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Jonouchi Targeted
Team Play for Victory

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:11.420
Duel, standby!

00:22:14.290 --> 00:22:22.190
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:22.190 --> 00:22:31.140
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:36.110
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:36.110 --> 00:22:40.080
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:40.510 --> 00:22:48.050
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:51.620
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:56.390
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:56.390 --> 00:23:06.500
And walk it without stopping

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:14.110
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:14.340 --> 00:23:23.080
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:31.060
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:31.060 --> 00:23:40.900
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
